"_score_accruals":59.7,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.1181417230013114,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":80.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.07050263718096045,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":11.9,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.12856817941977483,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":91.4,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11052268047790537,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":80.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04239798895758324,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":58.2,"_gate_share_shrink":0.11123154048379402,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":1.95312275606301e-05,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":100.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.02779,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Provident Financial Services, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for Provident Bank that provides various banking products and services to individuals, families, and businesses in the United States. Its deposit products include savings, checking, interest-bearing checking, money market deposit, and certificate of deposit accounts, as well as IRA products. The company's loan portfolio comprises commercial real estate loans that are secured by properties, such as multi-family apartment buildings, retail and industrial properties, and office buildings; commercial business loans; fixed-rate and adjustable-rate mortgage loans collateralized by one- to four-family residential real estate properties; residential mortgage loans; commercial construction loans; and consumer loans consisting of home equity loans, home equity lines of credit, personal loans and unsecured lines of credit, and auto and recreational vehicle loans. It also offers cash management, remote deposit capture, payroll origination, escrow account management, and online and mobile banking services; and business credit cards. In addition, the company provides wealth management services comprising investment management, trust and estate administration, financial planning, and tax compliance and planning; and insurance agency operations. Further, it sells insurance and investment products, including annuities; and manages and sells real estate properties acquired through foreclosure. The company was founded in 1839 and is headquartered in Jersey City, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony J. Labozzetta | President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $479K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $237K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Provident Financial Services, I is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.0B market cap on $870M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $431M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 49 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.4% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","22 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of PFS and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/Behavioral_Patterns_of_PFS_and_Institutional_Flows_111326125402_1794549242.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794549242.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"[Video Enhanced] West Red Lake Gold CEO Discusses Integrated Madsen Mine and Rowan Project PFS","source":"thenewswire.com","link":"https://www.thenewswire.com/press-releases/1BglFDvE6-video-enhanced-west-red-lake-gold-ceo-discusses-integrated-madsen-mine-and-rowan-project-pfs.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794227400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Provident Financial Services, Inc. (NYSE:PFS) Looks Like A Good Stock, And It's Going Ex-Dividend Soon","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-pfs/provident-financial-services/news/provident-financial-services-inc-nysepfs-looks-like-a-good-s","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794140736.2,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Provident Financial Services (PFS) On Q3 Results, Is The Pullback A Buying Opportunity?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/provident-financial-services-pfs-q3-171523720.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793812523.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.92,"tier":0,"scop